articles.content_en:
After reproductive material of an authorized variety has been sold by the variety right holder or by a unit or individual licensed by the variety right holder, if the right holder claims that another person's production, reproduction, or sale of such reproductive material constitutes infringement, the People's Court shall generally not uphold the claim, except in the following circumstances:
(1) producing, reproducing, or selling reproductive material obtained after production or reproduction of such reproductive material;
(2) exporting such reproductive material to a country or region that does not protect the plant genus or species to which the variety belongs, for the purpose of production or reproduction.

Where the alleged infringer claims that the following production or reproduction acts with respect to an authorized variety are scientific research activities, the People's Court shall uphold the claim:
(1) using the authorized variety to cultivate a new variety;
(2) after cultivating and forming a new variety by using the authorized variety, repeatedly using the reproductive material of the authorized variety for the needs of variety right application, variety examination, and variety registration.

Except for the circumstances provided for in relevant laws and judicial interpretations, the following circumstances may also be determined as serious circumstances of infringement:
(1) after being subjected to administrative penalty or being held liable by a court judgment for infringement, committing the same or similar infringing act again;
(2) engaging in infringement of variety rights as a business;
(3) forging a variety right certificate;
(4) selling authorized varieties in packaging without identification marks or labels;
(5) violating the provisions of Article 77, paragraph 1, items 1, 2, and 4 of the Seed Law;
(6) refusing to provide the location of production, reproduction, sale, and storage of the alleged infringing object.
Where the circumstances provided for in items 1 to 5 of the preceding paragraph exist, when punitive damages are applied according to law, the amount of punitive damages may be determined at not less than twice the calculation base.
